{"id":"memphis-lite","title":"Memphis Lite","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Memphis_Lite","rev":239173,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Memphis Lite"]}," (or ",{"t":"b","c":["Contempo-Eclectic"]},") is the corporatized, more stylized direct evolution of ",{"t":"a","c":["Memphis Design"],"id":"memphis-design"},". It arose because the latter was poorly suited to incorporate into existing home designs, and came to encompass graphic design and fashion more so than interior design. Memphis Lite was prevalent in popular culture from roughly 1984 to 1997, replacing ",{"t":"a","c":["Earth Tones"],"id":"earth-tones"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Supergraphic Ultramodern"],"id":"supergraphic-ultramodern"},". It overlapped with the mid-late 1980s ",{"t":"a","c":["Laser Grid"],"id":"laser-grid"}," aesthetic, and the early-mid 1990s ",{"t":"a","c":["Grunge"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Grunge"}," aesthetic. Memphis was succeeded in 1997-1998 by the ",{"t":"a","c":["Y2K Futurism"],"id":"y2k-futurism"}," aesthetic."]},{"t":"p","c":["Memphis Lite grew to become a ubiquitous aesthetic in popular culture, intermingling with other 80s-90s aesthetics such as Laser Grid, ",{"t":"a","c":["Wacky Pomo"],"id":"wacky-pomo"},", ",{"t":"a","c":["Factory Pomo"],"id":"factory-pomo"},", and ",{"t":"a","c":["Global Village Coffeehouse"],"id":"global-village-coffeehouse"},". Memphis Lite's complete overshadowing of the original Memphis Design in advertising, fashion and certain televisual works (such as game show sets) led to it supplanting the original in the public's memory, to the point that most Memphis revivals really harken to the Lite version, a peculiarity most noticeable with the color palette stereotypical of ",{"t":"a","c":["Synthwave"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Synthwave"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Vaporwave"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Vaporwave"},"."]}],"sections":[{"title":"History","id":"history","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Memphis Lite emerged in the mid-late 1980s as a diluted, consumer-grade iteration of the avant-garde ",{"t":"a","c":["Memphis Design"],"id":"memphis-design"}," movement. While true Memphis Design challenged traditional design norms with its bold colors, geometric shapes, and playful patterns, it was poorly suited to consumer products, and provided little thoughts in the real of graphic and fabric design. Memphis Lite came to overtake 1970s–early 1980s ",{"t":"a","c":["Earth Tones"],"id":"earth-tones"}," through more saturated colors and a less earthy palette, and soon incorporated elements of both contemporary and previous aesthetics."]},{"t":"p","c":["Notable borrowings include the chaotic arrangements and bold patterns of the ",{"t":"a","c":["Pacific Punk Wave"],"id":"pacific-punk-wave"},", and ",{"t":"a","c":["Googie"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Googie"}," elements such as misaligned borders and distinct groups of overlapping abstract shapes separate by blank space. Memphis lite also introduced ",{"t":"a","c":["art deco"],"id":"art-deco"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["cubist"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Cubism"}," figurative elements to an otherwise largely abstract design landscape. Other innovations of Memphis Lite include the \"scribbly\" and brushstroke motifs (as demonstrated by the iconic Jazz Cup design), illusory contours created by stippled or striped patterns forming shapes without outlines, and gradients, contrasting with Memphis' preference for flat colors and uninterrupted patterns."]},{"t":"p","c":["The aesthetic peaked around 1988 to 1993 with ",{"t":"i","c":["Saved by the Bell"]},", new jack swing's popularity, and the introduction of the ",{"t":"a","c":["jazz"],"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jazz_(design)"}," drinking cup style. During the early-mid-1990s, another aesthetic known as ",{"t":"a","c":["Global Village Coffeehouse"],"id":"global-village-coffeehouse"}," became popular, overlapping with Memphis in some aspects. ",{"t":"a","c":["Grunge"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Grunge"}," fashion and ",{"t":"a","c":["Corporate Grunge"],"id":"corporate-grunge"}," styles also appeared during this time and began overtaking Memphis Lite, though remnants of Memphis Lite continued into the mid-1990s."]},{"t":"p","c":["Memphis Lite's popularity faded around 1997-1998 and it was succeeded by the ",{"t":"a","c":["Y2K Futurism"],"id":"y2k-futurism"}," era. Some commercial establishments (such as Taco Bell, the Target Food Avenue, and various malls) continued to have the Memphis style until the mid-2010s, when they were redesigned in a ",{"t":"a","c":["Minimalist"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Minimalism"}," fashion. The Memphis Lite aesthetic is often used to retroactively define and depict the '80s and Early '90s, via ",{"t":"a","c":["retrofuturism"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Retrofuturism"}," such as ",{"t":"a","c":["Synthwave"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Synthwave"},", ",{"t":"a","c":["Vaporwave"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Vaporwave"},", and ",{"t":"a","c":["Future Funk"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Future_Funk"},"."]}]},{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Either of different palettes:"],"sub":[{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Bold flat primaries"]},{"c":["Subdued or pastel colors"]},{"c":["CMYK shades, particularly the combination of of at least two of teal/aqua, pink/magenta and purple"]}]}]},{"c":["Irregular stippled patterns with dots, irregular dashes or other shapes like triangles"]},{"c":["Illusory contours from striped or stippled patterns"]},{"c":["Stippled gradients"]},{"c":["Misaligned Googie borders"]},{"c":["Solid drop shadows"]},{"c":["Two types of patterns:"],"sub":[{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Busy, abstract patterns covering the entire planes (these were especially prominent in furniture design)"]},{"c":["Patterns composed of asymmetrical assemblages of shapes where each groups forms a separate unit on a flat or subdued pattern background (i.e. stipples)"]}]}]},{"c":["Outlined, typically rough-edged script fonts (",{"t":"a","c":["Corporate Grunge"],"id":"corporate-grunge"}," influences), often combined with a blockier font"]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Art Deco"],"id":"art-deco"},"-like combinations of dots, circles and lines"]},{"c":["Art Deco or cubist decorative pieces"]},{"c":["Heavy use of glass and chrome as a design element"]},{"c":["Abstract statement pieces combining all of the above in a cubic or abstract expressionist framework"]}]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Interior design in sitcoms and movies continued to focus on the same aesthetics that Memphis failed to replace, reflecting the failure of Memphis Lite to impose itself in consumer interior design. Like its predecessor, Memphis Lite found much more success in commercial spaces like malls and stores and in set designs for talk or game shows. Advertisements also made large use of the aesthetic. Some of these examples may also overlap with ",{"t":"a","c":["Wacky Pomo"],"id":"wacky-pomo"},"."]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Television"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["MTV"]}," (1981-1996)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Let's Make a Deal"]}," (1984-1986)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["WWF Golden Era"]}," (1984-1993)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["The Wuzzles"]}," (1984-1985)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Jem"]}," (1985-1988)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Remote Control"]}," (1987-1990)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Bumper Stumpers"]}," (Canada, 1987-1990)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Doctor Who"]}," (Sylvester McCoy era, 1987-1989)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Beverly Hills Teens"]}," (1987)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Mighty Mouse: The New Adventures"]}," (1987-1988)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Hey Vern, It's Ernest!"]}," (1988)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Talk About"]}," (Canada, 1988-1990)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Saved by the Bell"]}," (1989-1993)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air"]}," (1990–1996)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Fox Kids"]}," (1990-1998 era)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Yo Yogi!"]}," (1991)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Doug"]}," (1991-1994)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Nick Arcade"]}," (1992)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["California Dreams"]}," (1992–1996)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Adventures of Sonic the Hedgehog"]}," (1993–1996)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Rocko's Modern Life"]}," (1993-1996; 2019)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers"]}," (1993-1996)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Piment fort"]}," (Canada, 1993-2001)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["The Pink Panther"]}," (1993-1995)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["WWF New Generation Era"]}," (1993-1997)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["4 et demi..."]}," (Canada, 1994-2001, credits/logo design)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Life with Loopy"]}," (1996-2000)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Cow and Chicken"]}," (1997-1999)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["OK K.O.: Let's Be Heroes"]}," (2017-2019)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Bullet Time"]}," (2025)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Film"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Dirty Dancing"]}," (1987)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Just Temporary"]}," (TV movie, 1989)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Encino Man"]}," (1992)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["A Goofy Movie"]}," (1995)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Driving Mr. Pink"]}," (1995)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Space Jam"]}," (1996)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Music"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Paul Simon - \"You Can Call Me Al\" (1986)"]},{"c":["Tiffany - \"You and Me\" (animated sequence in the Jetsons, 1990)"]},{"c":["Paula Abdul - \"Opposites Attract\" (1990)"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Graphic design"]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/9/9f/2018-SH-Eddies-Supras-Santini-Trevor-Ryan_115.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223043909","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Pete Santini Paintjob, 1997"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/81/2018-SH-Eddies-Supras-Santini-Trevor-Ryan_122.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223043910","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/b/ba/Memphis8.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20220807020952","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["The \"jazz\" drinking cup designs that were popular in this era"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/5/5b/HT_paper_cup_jef_150624_16x9_992.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042827","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/a/a3/Original_1a38c388ac41ef8068d1c54fe509a859.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223045003","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["More brustroke and abstract scribble lines"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/f/fb/Original_bf5b3c92c2e1a66efbbbe1447bb530ff.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223045009","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/e4/Paris-france-april-16-2022-600w-2146468723.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223050008","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Vintage Polly Pocket toys with heavy use of the CMYK colors"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/42/Opposite_attracts.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223043911","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Paula Abdul - \"Opposites Attract\" (1990)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/d/d0/R-959234-1394132440-1325.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042830","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Exposé - \"Let Me Be The One\" (1987)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/76/R-645573-1269538183.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223045010","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Lisa Boray – \"Break It Out\" (1983)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/ce/R-1265987-1204928488.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223045012","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Bright primaries"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/8d/Ratio3x2_960.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223050006","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Duran Duran - ",{"t":"i","c":["Rio"]}," (1982)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/f/f2/5e385565a93d57c630d296e7d1651736.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042825","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/ea/Quatre_et_demi.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042827","w":185,"h":168,"cap":["Restrained, but typical use of layered, asymetrical shapes and gradiants"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/1/1c/Efa251124a01db235e464fcdc2bc84ff.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240224023036","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["One of several movies that made use of grunge-like scripts combined with repeated layers"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/1/1c/EPsxVvSXkAIfH7C.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042828","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Car pinstripes and accent stripes were a natural habitat for Memphis Lite"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/7e/Fa44b9b36e06853c3e4d2775beac75811.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042828","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Blocking and irregular stript letters, thick outlines, bright primaries... yes this is early Memphis Lite"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/35/CAREWORN.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042828","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Painting by Gary Spearin"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/67/Best-90s-movies-a-goofy-movie-1589565888.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042828","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/1/1f/4665382c50ea466c7bb5b1b6ba04b7dd-393x550.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042826","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/80/1446817543220.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20220809225427","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/c1/Jp.webp/revision/latest?cb=20221224051652","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/82/Original_5c27bcce3fea57b4f77e2684317475e1.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223045001","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["With a touch of Abstract Expresionnism"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/71/90s_statement_art.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223050009","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Gregory Gioiosa, ",{"t":"i","c":["Asterope"]}," (1988)",{"t":"br"},"An exuberant piece with all the Memphis Lite hallmarks"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/c2/Memphis_coffee_house.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240224042618","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Borrowing some elements of ",{"t":"a","c":["Global Village Coffeehouse"],"id":"global-village-coffeehouse"}]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Interior design"]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/89/Portland_International_Airport_carpet%2C_2015.JPG/revision/latest?cb=20240223042831","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["The ",{"t":"a","c":["Portland International Airport carpet"],"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portland_International_Airport_carpet"}," (right), another Memphis Lite design icon"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/c6/Piment_fort.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042827","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Despite its lateness, the ",{"t":"i","c":["Piment Fort"]}," set straddles the line between unadulterated Memphis and the implied playfulness of Memphis Lite"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/38/Hq720.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042828","w":185,"h":185,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Talk About"]}]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/00/Bumper_stumpers.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042828","w":185,"h":185,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Bumper Stumpers"]}]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/64/D8cf8c57-ac9b-4dd2-9c6e-07fdc11b11d2.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223042831","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["A darker version of the CMYK palette"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/b/b5/Original_fb6a80b14c11412c92641859cc740f5a.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223045509","w":185,"h":185,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Just Temporary"]}," (1989)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/00/Original_661c75513ec8d048d3522832f013942d.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223045704","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Glass Relief of Yokohama Station Subway, Cho Kyong Hee, 1993"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/2/29/Original_cf8fa0a4432c253e8dee43f59eef3096.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223045712","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Typical groups of Memphis Lite shapes (Dino's Cafe, La Jolla, CA, prior to 1996)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/42/Original_240fca4a13b36ea7481ef3ed223aa9dd.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223045711","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["With unusually heavy-handed Googie influence, bordering on ",{"t":"a","c":["Wacky Pomo"],"id":"wacky-pomo"}," (Carrie Brockman's Design Group)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/ca/Brochure-p2-1.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223045844","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Lindsey Balkweill ceramics"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/6d/March-2-2017-bozeman-montana-600w-692618209.png/revision/latest?cb=20240224034227","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Food Avenue Express in Bozeman, Montana with originals Lori Koopi 90s neons"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/f/fa/Memphis11.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20220807201807","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Former White Flint Mall in North Bethesda, Maryland"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Fashion and fabric design"]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/7b/90s_couch.JPG/revision/latest?cb=20240223043910","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Couches were often the most visible Memphis Lite element of a home decor"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/ee/Bad_sofa.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223042829","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/e2/90s_retro_shirt.png/revision/latest?cb=20240223043912","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["A genuine vintage 90s shirt"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/61/Best-90s-movies-zenon-1589565894.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042828","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Logo design with some 60s influence"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/c2/Dustin-diamond-then.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042828","w":185,"h":185,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Saved by the Bell"]}]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/80/MV5BMzFiNmUyNzEtMjIyNy00NDYwLTk4ZjItMjQyYzBjOGZkYTZkXkEyXkFqcGdeQXVyNTA1NDY3NzY%40._V1_.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042828","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["A character from ",{"t":"i","c":["4 et demi..."]}]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Music videos"]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/5/5c/The_Jetsons_Movie_-_You_and_Me_Animated_Sequence/revision/latest?cb=20240223050746","w":185,"h":139,"cap":["The video cycles through almost all the iterations and variants of Memphis Lite"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/b/b0/Lost_TV_Themes-_1989_Lisa_Kudrow_TV_movie_Just_Temporary%2C_hip-hop%21/revision/latest?cb=20240223050825","w":185,"h":139},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/4a/Paula_Abdul_-_Opposites_Attract_%28Official_Music_Video%29-2/revision/latest?cb=20240223050817","w":185,"h":139},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/ee/Paul_Simon_-_You_Can_Call_Me_Al_%28Official_Video%29/revision/latest?cb=20240224040509","w":185,"h":139},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/d/d1/Expos%C3%A9_-_Let_Me_Be_The_One/revision/latest?cb=20240224040448","w":185,"h":139},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/cf/Friends_-_Opening_Season_1/revision/latest?cb=20250124195407","w":185,"h":139}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Revival"]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/f/f9/Martin_Solveig_%26_GTA_-_Intoxicated_%28Official_Music_Video%29/revision/latest?cb=20250608015257","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Martin Solveig & GTA - Intoxicated (2015)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/38/F5d08a010f872a5f09bcba8231953fdb-1-440x550.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042827","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/c2/Tumblr_fafe35f53195b6704f4a0e6d06b7cb33_6b8f965e_1280.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240223042829","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/f/f0/Memphis3.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20210719074210","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/c8/Memphis4.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20210719074218","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/02/Memphis5.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20210719074227","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/5/5b/Memphis6.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20210719074236","w":185,"h":185}]}]}]}